<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Shanghai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1937</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sino-japanese-war">Second Sino-Japanese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a> was fought from August to November 1937 in and around Shanghai, the first major battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-sino-japanese-war">Second Sino-Japanese War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a> committed many of his best German-trained divisions, which held out for three months at a cost of very heavy casualties. Japanese landings at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a> Bay forced a Chinese retreat that opened the way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-shanghai.jpg" alt="Battle of Shanghai" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shanghai1937KMT_machine_gun_nest.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
